  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ISSB and the Pan African Federation of Accountants (PAFA) join forces to empower Africa Accountants for a Sustainable Future.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Sustainability Standards Board (ISSB) is an independent, private-sector body that develops and approves IFRS Sustainability Disclosure Standards. The ISSB&#x2019;s Partnership Framework for Capacity Building in Developing and Emerging Economies launched in 2022 and saw PAFA join forces with the ISSB to empower African accountants to apply newly developed sustainability standards. PAFA&#x2019;s local expertise extends to 125,000 African accountants, across 56 professional accountancy organisations in 45 African countries. In 2023 the ISSB finalised the first two non-financial standards on general sustainability and climate (IFRS S1 and IFRS S2) and is starting work with jurisdictions and companies to support adoption.
 
PAFA together with the ISSB&#x2019;s Partnership Framework, will support for the first phase of its capacity building work to empower 125,000 African accountants on IFRS S1 and IFRS S2 Standards to create a sustainable future for the African continent.</narrative>
  </description>
